# The Test Cabinet — web console environment file (`@clockwyrks/web`).
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values:
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Vite inlines only variables prefixed with `VITE_` into the browser bundle at
# build time. `.env.local` is gitignored; this `.env.example` is committed with
# placeholder/optional values only. Never put a real secret here — anything that
# reaches the browser is public.
#
# NOTE: the console names no service URL. It addresses `/api`, `/artifacts` and
# `/arena` of its own origin: the edge in a deployment, and in development the dev
# server's proxy to the `make -C deployments/local local-forward` services on
# localhost (aim it elsewhere with TCAB_PROXY_* in `.env.development.local`; see
# `.env.development`). This file documents the optional telemetry vars.

# ── Telemetry (OpenTelemetry / OTLP) ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Telemetry is OPT-IN. With VITE_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT unset (the
# default), the web console emits no browser telemetry. Set the endpoint to
# export browser traces over OTLP/HTTP.
#
# The local Grafana LGTM stack runs IN THE k3d CLUSTER (deployments/k8s/
# components/observability), not the devcontainer. The browser runs outside that
# cluster, so forward the in-cluster collector to localhost with
# `make -C deployments/local local-grafana` and point the bundle at the HTTP port
# (:4318 — the browser cannot use the gRPC :4317 port). Mirrors the Rust binaries'
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT, but must be VITE_-prefixed to reach the bundle.
#VITE_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318

# OTel service.name reported for browser telemetry. Default: tcab-web
#VITE_OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=tcab-web

# Sets the `deployment.environment.name` resource attribute. Default: local
#VITE_TCAB_ENV=local
